ry> </address> </addressbook> </applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANKIO CHEMICAL CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINTOU TAICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUDA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEUCHI, FUMIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANKIO CHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINTOU, TAICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUDA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEUCHI FUMIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINTOU TAICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUDA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEUCHI, FUMIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINTOU, TAICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUDA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for the production of 2-pyridylpyridine derivatives usable as intermediates of drugs or agricultural chemicals, which neither involves the use of an expensive metal catalyst nor causes environmental pollution and can be carried out even on an industrial scale. This process comprises the step (A) of preparing an amidrazone compound from a cyanated heterocyclic compound in an aqueous solvent, the step (B) of preparing a 1,2,4-triazine compound from the amidrazone compound in an aqueous solvent, and the step (C) of preparing a 2-pyridylpyridine derivative from the triazine compound.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production de dérivés de 2-pyridylpyridine pouvant être utilisés comme intermédiaires de médicaments ou comme produits chimiques agricoles. Ce procédé n'exige pas de catalyseur coûteux ni d'équipement spécial; il ne cause pas de pollution environnementale et peut même être utilisé à l'échelle industrielle. Ledit procédé consiste (A) à préparer un composé d'amidrazone à partir d'un composé hétérocyclique cyanisé dans un solvant aqueux, (B) à préparer un composé de 1,2,4-triazine à partir du composé amidrazone dans un solvant aqueux, et (C) à préparer un dérivé de 2-pyridylpyridine à partir dudit composé de triazine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>